#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""teamctl - minimal, provider-agnostic agent-teammate control on tmux.

Usage:

    teamctl                      # bare: open the default lead session
    teamctl init [--custom] [--yes]
    teamctl settings
    teamctl doctor
    teamctl lead on|off|status [--hook] [--cli claude|codex|grok|gemini|all]
    teamctl config [<dotted.key> [<value>]] [--menu]
    teamctl models [provider]
    teamctl spawn <role> [--provider claude|codex|grok|gemini|shell] [--prompt TEXT] [--cwd DIR]
    teamctl list
    teamctl status [role] [--json] [--watch [--interval N]]
    teamctl send <role> "<instruction>" [--no-enter]
    teamctl dispatch <role> --provider P --task "…" [--context-file F] [--model M] [--effort E]
    teamctl result <role> [--wait]
    teamctl followup <role> --task "…"
    teamctl route <role> --task "…" [--providers claude,codex,grok,gemini] [--dry-run]
    teamctl land <role> [--checkpoint-only] [--into BRANCH] [--dry-run] [--json]
    teamctl worktree list|prune [--json] [--dry-run]
    teamctl resurrect [role …] [--dry-run] [--yes]
    teamctl providers
    teamctl usage [--json] [--probe [provider|all]]
    teamctl update [--check]
    teamctl uninstall [--yes]
    teamctl shutdown <role>
    teamctl --version

Every teammate is a tmux pane running a provider CLI. The lead (this process)
never edits a teammate's work; it only spawns, lists, and cleanly shuts down.

Providers share one launch shape -- `<cmd> [flags] "<prompt>"` starts an
interactive session seeded with the prompt -- so Claude Code, Codex, Grok,
and Gemini CLI all get the same tmux + teammate capability, and a
[providers.custom.*] config block teaches teamctl any other CLI that
speaks the same shape (no code change needed).

State lives in a small JSON file (default ~/.local/state/agent-team/state.json,
override with $TEAMCTL_STATE). Access is serialized with an flock so concurrent
`spawn`/`shutdown` calls can't race and orphan a pane. Nothing global or
system-level is touched.
"""

