# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# the provider-spec registry — every provider, built-in OR user-defined via
# a [providers.custom.*] block in config.toml, is DATA in one schema; the
# adapter functions (headless_argv / resume_argv / interactive_flags /
# _extract_session_id / provider_auth_state) are thin template expanders
# over it. Adding a provider means adding a spec, not editing seven
# if-chains.
#
# argv templates: "{task}", "{model}", "{effort}", "{session_id}" are
# substituted INSIDE argv tokens. Values only ever land in argv slots (and
# are shlex-quoted wholesale when a pane command line is built) — no shell
# ever interpolates them.
#
# Spec fields:
#   argv               interactive launch prefix (a positional prompt may
#                      be appended by build_launch_line)
#   headless           one-shot dispatch argv; absent -> dispatch/route
#                      refuse (a spawn-only provider)
#   resume             exact-session follow-up argv; absent -> followup
#                      refuses (teamctl never guesses "most recent")
#   model_args         appended when a model is set
#   effort_args        appended when an effort is set; None/missing means
#                      the CLI has no effort control — teamctl DROPS the
#                      effort with a one-line stderr note, never silently
#   resume_takes_model whether resume re-sends the model flags (codex: no;
#                      effort is never re-sent on resume — v0.4.0 behavior)
#   session_source     where the exact session id comes from:
#                        {"type": "result-json", "key": K}  recursive key
#                           lookup over the result/error JSON artifacts
#                        {"type": "stderr-regex", "pattern": P, ...}
#                           group 1 of P over error.log ("uuid": True
#                           validates the match; "fallback" names a
#                           built-in fallback strategy)
#                      None -> no capture (followup refuses; the shell
#                      test provider is the deliberate sessionless case)
#   auth_env /         signed-in detection: exported key(s) count as
#   auth_env_extra /   signed in; auth_files are login artifacts (parse-
#   auth_files         able non-empty JSON -> signed in, unreadable ->
#                      "unknown", never guessed)
#   login_hint /       the lattice's advice strings for locked-out /
#   wake_hint          quiet providers
#   probe              hidden TUI usage probe ({"argv", "command",
#                      "extra_enters"}); absent -> `usage --probe` refuses
#   routable           participates in route/usage/providers tables
#   quiet_flags        (shell only) silently ignore model/effort — it is
#                      the tmux-mechanics test provider, not an AI CLI
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

